{"id":"mahabharata-9-053","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":53,"title":"त्रिपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 53 · Balarama comes to the Samantapanchaka","summary":{"en":"Balarama sees Kurukshetra and gives gifts at the tirthas, and Narada tells him that the Kauravas are fighting a great war. Balarama hurries on his swift chariot to see the battle between Duryodhana and Bhima.","kn":"ಬಲರಾಮ ಕುರುಕ್ಷೇತ್ರ ನೋಡಿ ತೀರ್ಥಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ದಾನ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೌರವರು ಮಹಾಯುದ್ಧ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಿದ್ದಾರೆಂದು ನಾರದ ಅವನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ-ಭೀಮರ ಯುದ್ಧ ನೋಡಲು ಬಲರಾಮ ವೇಗದ ರಥದಲ್ಲಿ ಧಾವಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"बलराम कुरुक्षेत्र देखकर तीर्थों में दान देते हैं, और नारद उन्हें बताते हैं कि कौरव महायुद्ध कर रहे हैं। बलराम दुर्योधन-भीम का युद्ध देखने के लिए तेज़ रथ पर दौड़ पड़ते हैं।","te":"బలరాముడు కురుక్షేత్రాన్ని చూసి తీర్థాలలో దానాలు ఇస్తాడు; కౌరవులు మహా యుద్ధం చేస్తున్నారని నారదుడు అతనికి చెబుతాడు. దుర్యోధన భీముల పోరు చూడటానికి బలరాముడు వేగవంతమైన రథంపై వస్తాడు.","ta":"பலராமன் குருக்ஷேத்திரத்தைக் கண்டு தீர்த்தங்களில் தானம் அளிக்க, கௌரவர் பெரும்போர் புரிகின்றனர் என்று நாரதர் கூறுகிறார். துரியோதன பீமரின் போரைக் காணப் பலராமன் விரைந்த தேரில் வருகிறான்.","ml":"ബലരാമൻ കുരുക്ഷേത്രം കാണുകയും തീർത്ഥങ്ങളിൽ ദാനം നൽകുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു; കൗരവർ മഹായുദ്ധം ചെയ്യുന്നുവെന്ന് നാരദൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തോട് പറയുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനനും ഭീമനും തമ്മിലുള്ള യുദ്ധം കാണാൻ ബലരാമൻ വേഗമേറിയ രഥത്തിൽ തിടുക്കത്തിൽ പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.53; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"सारस्वतपर्व","titleEn":"Sarasvata Parva (Balarama's pilgrimage on the Sarasvati)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कुरुक्षेत्रं ततो दृष्ट्वा दत्त्वा दायांश्च सात्वतः ।\nआश्रमं सुमहद्दिव्यमगमज्जनमेजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having seen Kurukshetra and given gifts, the Sathvata chief Balarama came, O Janamejaya, to a great and divine hermitage."}},{"n":2,"text":"मधूकाम्रवनोपेतं प्लक्षन्यग्रोधसंकुलम् ।\nचिरिबिल्वयुतं पुण्यं पनसार्जुनसंकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was holy, with groves of madhuka and mango, crowded with plaksha and nyagrodha trees, with chiribilva, jackfruit and arjuna trees."}},{"n":3,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा यादवश्रेष्ठः प्रवरं पुण्यलक्षणम् ।\nपप्रच्छ तानृषीन्सर्वान्कस्याश्रमवरस्त्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that excellent place with its holy marks, the best of the Yadavas asked all the seers: \"Whose splendid hermitage is this?\""}},{"n":4,"text":"ते तु सर्वे महात्मानमूचू राजन्हलायुधम् ।\nशृणु विस्तरतो राम यस्यायं पूर्वमाश्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They all said to the great-souled plough-bearer, O king: \"Rama, hear in detail whose hermitage this was in the past.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"अत्र विष्णुः पुरा देवस्तप्तवांस्तप उत्तमम् ।\nअत्रास्य विधिवद्यज्ञाः सर्वे वृत्ताः सनातनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here long ago the god Vishnu practised supreme austerity, and here all his eternal sacrifices were duly performed.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"अत्रैव ब्राह्मणी सिद्धा कौमारब्रह्मचारिणी ।\nयोगयुक्ता दिवं याता तपःसिद्धा तपस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here too a perfected brahmin woman, a lifelong celibate, joined to yoga, went to heaven, perfected by austerity.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"बभूव श्रीमती राजञ्शाण्डिल्यस्य महात्मनः ।\nसुता धृतव्रता साध्वी नियता ब्रह्मचारिणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"She was the glorious, firm-vowed, virtuous and disciplined celibate daughter of the great-souled Shandilya, O king.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"सा तु प्राप्य परं योगं गता स्वर्गमनुत्तमम् ।\nभुक्त्वाश्रमेऽश्वमेधस्य फलं फलवतां शुभा ।\nगता स्वर्गं महाभागा पूजिता नियतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having attained supreme yoga, she went to the highest heaven; in this hermitage she enjoyed the fruit of the Ashvamedha, the best of fruits, and that fortunate woman went to heaven honoured by the self-controlled.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"अभिगम्याश्रमं पुण्यं दृष्ट्वा च यदुपुंगवः ।\nऋषींस्तानभिवाद्याथ पार्श्वे हिमवतोऽच्युतः ।\nस्कन्धावाराणि सर्वाणि निवर्त्यारुरुहेऽचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching that holy hermitage and seeing it, the bull of the Yadavas, Krishna's brother, bowed to those seers, sent back all his camps, and climbed the mountain near the Himalaya."}},{"n":10,"text":"नातिदूरं ततो गत्वा नगं तालध्वजो बली ।\nपुण्यं तीर्थवरं दृष्ट्वा विस्मयं परमं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going not far, the mighty palm-bannered Balarama came to a hill and, seeing a holy and excellent ford, was filled with great wonder."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रभवं च सरस्वत्याः प्लक्षप्रस्रवणं बलः ।\nसंप्राप्तः कारपचनं तीर्थप्रवरमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Balarama reached Plakshaprasravana, the source of the Sarasvati, and Karapachana, an excellent and supreme ford."}},{"n":12,"text":"हलायुधस्तत्र चापि दत्त्वा दानं महाबलः ।\nआप्लुतः सलिले शीते तस्माच्चापि जगाम ह ।\nआश्रमं परमप्रीतो मित्रस्य वरुणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too the mighty plough-bearer gave gifts, bathed in the cool water, and from there went, greatly pleased, to the hermitage of Mitra and Varuna."}},{"n":13,"text":"इन्द्रोऽग्निरर्यमा चैव यत्र प्राक्प्रीतिमाप्नुवन् ।\nतं देशं कारपचनाद्यमुनायां जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"He went from Karapachana to that place on the Yamuna where Indra, Agni and Aryaman had once found delight."}},{"n":14,"text":"स्नात्वा तत्रापि धर्मात्मा परां तुष्टिमवाप्य च ।\nऋषिभिश्चैव सिद्धैश्च सहितो वै महाबलः ।\nउपविष्टः कथाः शुभ्राः शुश्राव यदुपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing there too, the righteous one reached great contentment; the mighty bull of the Yadavas sat with seers and Siddhas and listened to fine stories."}},{"n":15,"text":"तथा तु तिष्ठतां तेषां नारदो भगवानृषिः ।\nआजगामाथ तं देशं यत्र रामो व्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they sat so, the venerable sage Narada came to the place where Rama was seated."}},{"n":16,"text":"जटामण्डलसंवीतः स्वर्णचीरी महातपाः ।\nहेमदण्डधरो राजन्कमण्डलुधरस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was wrapped in a mass of matted hair, wore a golden garment, and was a great ascetic, O king, carrying a golden staff and a water-pot."}},{"n":17,"text":"कच्छपीं सुखशब्दां तां गृह्य वीणां मनोरमाम् ।\nनृत्ये गीते च कुशलो देवब्राह्मणपूजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He held his lovely lute with its sweet sound, skilled in dance and song, honoured by gods and brahmins."}},{"n":18,"text":"प्रकर्ता कलहानां च नित्यं च कलहप्रियः ।\nतं देशमगमद्यत्र श्रीमान्रामो व्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A maker of quarrels, always fond of quarrels, he came to the place where the glorious Rama was."}},{"n":19,"text":"प्रत्युत्थाय तु ते सर्वे पूजयित्वा यतव्रतम् ।\nदेवर्षिं पर्यपृच्छन्त यथावृत्तं कुरून्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them rose, honoured that ascetic of strict vows, and asked the divine seer how things had gone with the Kurus."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततोऽस्याकथयद्राजन्नारदः सर्वधर्मवित् ।\nसर्वमेव यथावृत्तमतीतं कुरुसंक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, Narada, who knew all dharma, told Rama everything that had happened, the destruction of the Kurus, which was now past."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीद्रौहिणेयो नारदं दीनया गिरा ।\nकिमवस्थं तु तत्क्षत्रं ये च तत्राभवन्नृपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the son of Rohini said to Narada in a sorrowful voice: \"In what state is that warrior order, and the kings who were there?\""}},{"n":22,"text":"श्रुतमेतन्मया पूर्वं सर्वमेव तपोधन ।\nविस्तरश्रवणे जातं कौतूहलमतीव मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I heard all this earlier, you whose wealth is austerity, but now I am very curious to hear it in full.\""}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"पूर्वमेव हतो भीष्मो द्रोणः सिन्धुपतिस्तथा ।\nहतो वैकर्तनः कर्णः पुत्राश्चास्य महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma was killed first, and Drona, and the lord of the Sindhus; Karna, son of Vikartana, was killed, and his mighty sons."}},{"n":24,"text":"भूरिश्रवा रौहिणेय मद्रराजश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nएते चान्ये च बहवस्तत्र तत्र महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Rohini's son, and the powerful king of the Madras, these and many other strong warriors were killed in various places."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रियान्प्राणान्परित्यज्य प्रियार्थं कौरवस्य वै ।\nराजानो राजपुत्राश्च समरेष्वनिवर्तिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings and princes who never turned back in battle gave up their dear lives for the sake of the Kaurava."}},{"n":26,"text":"अहतांस्तु महाबाहो शृणु मे तत्र माधव ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रबले शेषाः कृपो भोजश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nअश्वत्थामा च विक्रान्तो भग्नसैन्या दिशो गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O mighty-armed descendant of Madhu, hear who was not killed. In Dhritarashtra's army the survivors were Kripa, the powerful Bhoja, and the valiant Ashvatthama, who fled in different directions with their army broken."}},{"n":27,"text":"दुर्योधनो हते सैन्ये प्रद्रुतेषु कृपादिषु ।\nह्रदं द्वैपायनं नाम विवेश भृशदुःखितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the army was destroyed and Kripa and the others had fled, Duryodhana, deeply grieved, entered the lake called Dvaipayana."}},{"n":28,"text":"शयानं धार्तराष्ट्रं तु स्तम्भिते सलिले तदा ।\nपाण्डवाः सह कृष्णेन वाग्भिरुग्राभिरार्दयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana lay there with the water held still; the Pandavas, with Krishna, tormented him with harsh words."}},{"n":29,"text":"स तुद्यमानो बलवान्वाग्भी राम समन्ततः ।\nउत्थितः प्राग्घ्रदाद्वीरः प्रगृह्य महतीं गदाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pained on all sides by those words, O Rama, the mighty hero rose from the lake, taking up a great mace."}},{"n":30,"text":"स चाप्युपगतो युद्धं भीमेन सह सांप्रतम् ।\nभविष्यति च तत्सद्यस्तयो राम सुदारुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He has now come to fight Bhima, and at this moment, Rama, a terrible battle between the two will take place."}},{"n":31,"text":"यदि कौतूहलं तेऽस्ति व्रज माधव मा चिरम् ।\nपश्य युद्धं महाघोरं शिष्ययोर्यदि मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you are curious, descendant of Madhu, go without delay; watch that very terrible battle of your two pupils, if you think fit."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"नारदस्य वचः श्रुत्वा तानभ्यर्च्य द्विजर्षभान् ।\nसर्वान्विसर्जयामास ये तेनाभ्यागताः सह ।\nगम्यतां द्वारकां चेति सोऽन्वशादनुयायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Narada's words, Balarama honoured those best of brahmins and dismissed all who had come with him, telling his followers: \"Go to Dvaraka.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"सोऽवतीर्याचलश्रेष्ठात्प्लक्षप्रस्रवणाच्छुभात् ।\nततः प्रीतमना रामः श्रुत्वा तीर्थफलं महत् ।\nविप्राणां संनिधौ श्लोकमगायदिदमच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, coming down from the best of mountains, the auspicious Plakshaprasravana, Rama, pleased at hearing the great reward of the sacred fords, sang this verse in the presence of the brahmins."}},{"n":34,"text":"सरस्वतीवाससमा कुतो रतिः\nसरस्वतीवाससमाः कुतो गुणाः ।\nसरस्वतीं प्राप्य दिवं गता जनाः\nसदा स्मरिष्यन्ति नदीं सरस्वतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where is there delight equal to living on the Sarasvati? Where are there virtues equal to living on the Sarasvati? People who have reached the Sarasvati and gone to heaven will always remember the river Sarasvati.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"सरस्वती सर्वनदीषु पुण्या\nसरस्वती लोकसुखावहा सदा ।\nसरस्वतीं प्राप्य जनाः सुदुष्कृताः\nसदा न शोचन्ति परत्र चेह च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Sarasvati is the holiest of all rivers; the Sarasvati always brings happiness to the world; people of great sins who reach the Sarasvati never grieve, here or hereafter.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"ततो मुहुर्मुहुः प्रीत्या प्रेक्षमाणः सरस्वतीम् ।\nहयैर्युक्तं रथं शुभ्रमातिष्ठत परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, gazing again and again with love at the Sarasvati, the scorcher of foes mounted a splendid chariot yoked with horses."}},{"n":37,"text":"स शीघ्रगामिना तेन रथेन यदुपुंगवः ।\nदिदृक्षुरभिसंप्राप्तः शिष्ययुद्धमुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that swift chariot the bull of the Yadavas, eager to see it, arrived where the battle of his pupils had begun."}}]}]}